    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.5vw,36px);margin:0 0 32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">Do you charge extra to come out to Memramcook?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">No. Memramcook sits right between Moncton and Sackville, just off Route 2, so it's inside our regular service area. Your free written estimate covers the full job, travel included, with no surprise fees.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">My insurance company wants my Memramcook oil tank replaced. How fast can you do it?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">In most cases we can replace a tank within a few days of your call, and the swap itself is usually done in a day. You get a new CSA-approved tank plus the documentation your insurer needs to renew your policy. If your renewal deadline is tight, tell us and we'll do our best to move things up.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">We bought an older farmhouse in the valley. How do we know if there's a buried oil tank?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Look for a fill pipe or vent line near the foundation that doesn't connect to your current tank, or old copper oil lines coming through the basement wall. Those are classic signs of an abandoned underground tank. We can locate it, confirm what's down there, and remove it with proper documentation for your insurer and lawyer.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 10px;">Can you reach Memramcook in winter if my tank starts leaking?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes. Route 2 and Route 106 keep the valley reachable year-round, and our emergency line runs 24/7. Call (506) 802-3471 the moment you smell oil or see a drip, because a small leak in January turns into a big cleanup fast.</p>
